        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18311389?u=9ca7c2bf96b915fc275cfcb658fc3fb9ee2f1e0c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Change-set updates chromium support notes for <code class=\"notranslate\">chrome_settings_overrides</code> given that it only has implementations for Windows and MacOS. Version numbers have also been updated to represent more precisely when these features where added.<br>\nNext to this chromium requirements for <code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider</code> properties have also been added as notes to the following properties;</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider.favicon_url</code>: Required and needs a HTTP or HTTPS URL which differs from Mozilla's implementation</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider.is_default</code>: Given it's a required property within chromium</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider.encoding</code>: Required in chromium when <code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider.prepopulated_id</code> is not provided.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Sources:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/manifest/chrome-settings-override\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/manifest/chrome-settings-override</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40717644#comment7\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40717644#comment7</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/caugner/chromium-releases/blob/v35/chrome/common/extensions/docs/templates/articles/settings_override.html#L17-L39\">https://github.com/caugner/chromium-releases/blob/v35/chrome/common/extensions/docs/templates/articles/settings_override.html#L17-L39</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/fe4521c72ade5144b6fb08dcc40afcaf62c67ec3/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/fe4521c72ade5144b6fb08dcc40afcaf62c67ec3\">chromium/chromium@<tt>fe4521c</tt></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/caugner/chromium-releases/blame/v58/chrome/common/extensions/api/manifest_types.json#L93-L97\">https://github.com/caugner/chromium-releases/blame/v58/chrome/common/extensions/api/manifest_types.json#L93-L97</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also see linked issue below.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #27046.\">closes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3141541483\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27046\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27046/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27046\">#27046</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27065",
            "title": "Corrected webextensions.manifest.chrome_settings_overrides for chrome",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-15T23:34:46.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-15T23:33:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Electrenator",
                "url": "https://github.com/Electrenator"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari on iOS 26 adds <code class=\"notranslate\">dns-prefetch</code> support. Before, it was only supported on macOS.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1236689303\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/16299\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/16299/hovercard?comment_id=2655788790&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/16299#issuecomment-2655788790\">#16299 (comment)</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #16299.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1236689303\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/16299\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/16299/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/16299\">#16299</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27057",
            "title": "Safari on iOS 26 adds `dns-prefetch` support",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-13T15:38:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-13T15:38:00.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds subfeatures for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/supportedValuesOf\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.supportedValuesOf()</code></a> for each <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/supportedValuesOf#parameters\" rel=\"nofollow\">accepted value</a> (cf. <a href=\"https://tc39.es/ecma402/#sec-intl.supportedvaluesof\" rel=\"nofollow\">the spec</a>), and a nested non-standard behavioral subfeature <code class=\"notranslate\">timeZone.includes_UTC</code> to account for the behavioral difference between Chrome and Firefox/Safari.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To confirm support of the subfeatures, I tested <a href=\"https://jsbin.com/vozekiwilo/1/edit?js,output\" rel=\"nofollow\">this JSBin</a> in Chrome 99, Firefox 93, and Safari 15.6 (assuming behavior hadn't changed since 15.4), and I tested the following in Deno 1.19 and Node 18.0.0:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"for (const value of [&quot;calendar&quot;, &quot;collation&quot;, &quot;currency&quot;, &quot;numberingSystem&quot;, &quot;timeZone&quot;, &quot;unit&quot;]) {\n  const output = Intl.supportedValuesOf(value);\n  console.log(value + &quot;: &quot; + (Array.isArray(output) &amp;&amp; output.length &gt; 0 ? &quot;OK&quot; : JSON.stringify(output)));\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">for</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">value</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">of</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-s\">\"calendar\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\"collation\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\"currency\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\"numberingSystem\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\"timeZone\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\"unit\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">output</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">Intl</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">supportedValuesOf</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">value</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">console</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">log</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">value</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">+</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\": \"</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">+</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-v\">Array</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">isArray</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">output</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">output</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">length</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span> ? <span class=\"pl-s\">\"OK\"</span> : <span class=\"pl-c1\">JSON</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">stringify</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">output</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To check support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">timeZone.includes_UTC</code> subfeature, I manually executed <code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.supportedValuesOf('timeZone').includes('UTC')</code> in Chrome 137, Deno 1.19.0 + 2.3.6, Firefox 93, Node.js 18.0.0 + 24.2.0, and Safari 15.6.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #25828.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2823819175\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25828\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25828/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25828\">#25828</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27056",
            "title": "Add `Intl.supportedValuesOf()` subfeatures",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-13T15:15:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-13T15:07:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Moves <code class=\"notranslate\">static_class_fields</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">static_initialization_blocks</code> from <code class=\"notranslate\">javascript.classes</code> into <code class=\"notranslate\">javascript.classes.static</code>, removing the <code class=\"notranslate\">static_</code> prefix.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #19102.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1619457362\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/19102\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/19102/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/19102\">#19102</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27055",
            "title": "Move javascript.classes.static_* under static.*",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-17T16:29:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-13T11:43:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This creates a PR to test the suggestion for structuring Reporting API report body types made in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3132335736\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27021\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27021/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27021\">#27021</a> - what was suggested there did not quite survive attempted rollout.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For context,</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>we currently a <code class=\"notranslate\">Report</code> API with properties <code class=\"notranslate\">type</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">body</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">url</code>.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">.body</code> can take an object that is derived from <code class=\"notranslate\">ReportBody</code> that differs based on the <code class=\"notranslate\">type</code>.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">Report</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">ReportBody</code>, and derived types such as <code class=\"notranslate\">InterventionReportBody</code> were originally IDL objects, which  means that previously we could document body types in the body interfaces, such as <code class=\"notranslate\">InterventionReportBody</code></li>\n<li>Now we have some body types that are dictionaries, some with no name at all. The plan is for <code class=\"notranslate\">ReportBody</code> and possibly even <code class=\"notranslate\">Report</code> to be dictionaries.</li>\n<li>Right now we agreed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3132335736\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27021\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27021/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27021\">#27021</a> that we can record the body type compat in <code class=\"notranslate\">Report</code>. Note that eventually this will probably have to go in <code class=\"notranslate\">ReportingObserver</code>. Yuck.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We have is a whole bunch of different string values for <code class=\"notranslate\">Report.type</code>. We also have a whole bunch of possible report body properties, which vary or might potentially vary by type.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/caugner/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/caugner\">@caugner</a> Generally we document all properties of the web API objects (not just the ones that have changed). Since these properties \"live\" in an object mapped to <code class=\"notranslate\">Report.body</code> that's where I've added them, grouped by type. So it looks like this:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"api.Report\n  .type\n  .body\n      type_coep # The body type. Inside here go all the properties.\n         type # Yes, the body itself also can have a type\n         destination # non-standard\n         disposition\n         blockedURL\n      type_csp-violation\n         - blocked_url\n         - columnNumber\n         - .... [not yet done]\n      type_all_the other_types\n    ...\n  .url\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">api.Report\n  .type\n  .body\n      type_coep # The body type. Inside here go all the properties.\n         type # Yes, the body itself also can have a type\n         destination # non-standard\n         disposition\n         blockedURL\n      type_csp-violation\n         - blocked_url\n         - columnNumber\n         - .... [not yet done]\n      type_all_the other_types\n    ...\n  .url\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that I haven't yet added all the properties for the other types such as <code class=\"notranslate\">type_csp-violation</code> - not worth it unless you agree this is the right approach.<br>\nLet me know.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work done in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3132245291\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39880\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/39880/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39880\">mdn/content#39880</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27047",
            "title": "Report type types coep",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-17T17:25:42.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-13T05:32:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add details of properties added to <code class=\"notranslate\">webNavigation.onCommitted</code> in Chrome in version 74 and 106.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Addresses the issue raised in <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39630#top\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/39630/hovercard\">webNavigation.onCommitted details does not mention discrepancy with Chromium</a> #39630 by providing clarification that these properties are only supported in Chrome.</p>",
